<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/8th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Marj Ardabil</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">730</span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a> · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arab-khazar-wars">Arab–Khazar wars</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Marj <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardabil">Ardabil</a> was fought in December 730 near Ardabil, in north-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iran">Iran</a>, between a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazar</a> army and the forces of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/umayyad-caliphate">Umayyad Caliphate</a>. The Khazars destroyed the Arab army and killed its commander, al-Jarrah ibn Abdallah al-Hakami, and then raided deep into the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliphate</a>'s lands as far as northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>. The defeat led the Umayyads to send larger armies to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caucasus">Caucasus</a> in the following years.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/battle-of-marj-ardabil.jpg" alt="Battle of Marj Ardabil" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: No machine-readable author provided. CrniBombarder!!! assumed (based on copyright claims). · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sab_dalj1.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
